 ## [Unreleased]
 
+### Added
+
+- `ToolRegistry.execute` now validates tool `input` against the resolved definition's `inputSchema` before calling the executor. It returns a rejection `ToolResponse` to the model when validation fails rather than throwing an error, allowing the model to correct the call within the turn.
+- A static tool definition's `inputSchema` is compiled synchronously at `register` time, throwing an error naming the tool if the schema is invalid JSON Schema.
+
+### Changed
+
+- Executors now receive only input that already satisfies `inputSchema`.
+
